# Kernel modules to copy into the initramfs.
#
# Intentionally empty for the Fairphone 2.
#
# Everything the citronics initramfs touches before pivot_root is built-in
# (=y) in linux-6.15.defconfig:
#
#   CONFIG_SQUASHFS=y / CONFIG_SQUASHFS_XZ=y   ← rootfs filesystem
#   CONFIG_EXT4_FS=y                            ← boot partition
#   CONFIG_F2FS_FS=y                            ← application-data partition
#   CONFIG_VFAT_FS / CONFIG_FAT_FS              ← (only =m, not needed at boot)
#   CONFIG_BLK_DEV_DM=y / CONFIG_DM_*           ← kpartx subpartition mapping
#   CONFIG_USB_GADGET=y / CONFIG_USB_ETH=y      ← USB recovery network
#
# The =m drivers in this system (modem QCOM_Q6V5_MSS, QRTR, FASTRPC,
# IIO_QCOM_SMGR*, …) all load AFTER pivot_root from the real rootfs, so they
# do not belong here — carrying extra .ko files only inflates the cpio.gz
# past lk2nd's max-initrd ceiling.
#
# If a future kernel revision flips one of the boot-critical options above to
# =m, list it here as a path relative to /lib/modules/<ver>/ — for example
#   kernel/fs/squashfs/squashfs.ko
